'''VRC BOXING''' is a cross-platform [[Special:MyLanguage/:Category:Game worlds|game world]] published by {{VRC link|https://vrchat.com/home/user/usr_7c418e52-2e68-434f-9ed1-3873941ab924|ムシコロリ}}. Players box with tracked punches. WOW Sports Entertainment Inc. (ワオスポーツ株式会社) runs the project.<ref name="about">[https://vrcboxing.com/about/ 会社情報] on ''vrcboxing.com''. Retrieved {{Date|2026-09-11}}.</ref>

== Layout ==

Players spawn in a gym lobby. Language select is EN (English), JP (Japanese), and KR (Korean). How to Play, World Settings, Update Notes, and a UI hub are near spawn.

A tutorial starts near spawn. Players pick [[File:VRC_BOXING_icon_-_3-point.png|24px|alt=3-point]] 3-point tracking or [[File:VRC_BOXING_icon_-_FBT.png|24px|alt=FBT]] FBT (full-body tracking), take a glove, and set the official height. Punch lessons cover Jab, Straight, Hook, and OneTwoHook. The tutorial also runs throwing and guarding drills of 20 punches each.

A Training Area has Daily Workout, Punching Test, SPEED STRIKE, and a Sparring Mat. Daily Workout assigns a daily task. Punching Test evaluates punch form on a dummy. SPEED STRIKE is a 30-second scoring drill against red markers. Points follow punch speed and power.<ref name="intro">[https://vrcboxing.com/2024/02/20/vrchatボクシングゲームワールド「vrc-boxing」の紹介/ VRChatボクシングゲームワールド「VRC BOXING」の紹介] on ''vrcboxing.com''. Dated {{Date|2024-02-20}}; retrieved {{Date|2026-09-11}}.</ref> A new SPEED STRIKE personal record can be uploaded to a global ranking. Achievements are tracked in the gym. On the Sparring Mat, players dodge balls from a coach and stay off an OUT line.

Each ring has Match Settings. Queue Mode can be Instant or Next. Players can switch rings. Tracking can be set to 3-point or FBT at the ring. A round timer can be stopped and started.

A commendation platform lists four labeled plates: Former WBC (World Boxing Council) World Flyweight Champion Daisuke Naito, Twitch streamer sutanmi, Robert YAMAMOTO, and Magical Lovely Noda. Naito's plate includes an autograph dated {{Date|2023-04-20}}. Further unlabeled portraits hangs on the same wall.

A G-SHOCK poster in the gym opens the G-SHOCK VRChat page in the browser.<ref name="gshock-casio">[https://gshock.casio.com/intl/virtual/vrchat/ G-SHOCK × VRChat] on ''gshock.casio.com''. Retrieved {{Date|2026-09-14}}.</ref> A G-SHOCK CUP collage hangs in the gym. The same series appears under [[Special:MyLanguage/List of Shop listings#G-SHOCK x VRChat|G-SHOCK x VRChat]] and [[Special:MyLanguage/Accessories|Accessories]].

The lobby has a VRC BOXING shop. A VIP Room opens for Gold, Platinum, and Diamond Supporter listings.

Players can open Official Teams and the group page. PUNCHLINE TRACKS plays selected tracks in the gym on a timer.<ref name="punchline">[https://vrcboxing.com/2026/04/11/vrc-boxing%e3%80%8cpunchline-tracks%e3%80%8d%e6%8e%b2%e8%bc%89%e6%a5%bd%e6%9b%b2%e3%82%a8%e3%83%b3%e3%83%88%e3%83%aa%e3%83%bc%e5%8f%97%e4%bb%98%e3%82%b9%e3%82%bf%e3%83%bc%e3%83%88/ VRC BOXING「PUNCHLINE TRACKS」掲載楽曲エントリー受付スタート] on ''vrcboxing.com''. Dated {{Date|2026-04-11}}; retrieved {{Date|2026-09-11}}.</ref>

== Gameplay ==

Players put on gloves, enter a ring, and start on the gong.<ref name="howto">[https://vrcboxing.com/howto/ HOW TO PLAY] on ''vrcboxing.com''. Retrieved {{Date|2026-09-11}}.</ref> Punches land on the head and body. Form and speed determine damage. Gloves and arms guard.

A Ring Owner can change Match Settings. Matches can be limited to All Platforms, Quest, or PC.

