When the set rounds finish, the match ends by decision or draw.

Rumble is a team match of up to four players (2v2, 1v3, 1v1v2, 3v1). Under 3v1, the solo player's health is multiplied by five.

HOW TO PLAY documents HP, STA, and GD for eSports Mode, and a Real Mode ruleset.<ref name="howto" />

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Meter
! eSports Mode
|-
| HP (health points)
| Starts at 50. Maximum falls 50 → 40 → 30 after knockdowns.
|-
| STA (stamina)
| Falls on Heavy Punch and body shots, then recovers. Overspend causes BREAK and slower movement. Low STA cuts outgoing damage and can TKO (technical knockout) on knockdown.
|-
| GD (guard)
| Right-stick-down guard, at most two times in a row. Attacking recovers GD. The player cannot attack while guarding. GUA is the HOW TO PLAY name for GD.
|}

Heavy Punch is a held button that spends stamina. From round 2 onward, Mega Punch unlocks after 12 punch hits.

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Real Mode<br>Standard
|-
| 2-minute rounds, 10-second interval
|-
| Remaining HP decides the winner
|-
| 3-knockdown TKO
|-
| Guard covers from glove to shoulder
|-
| No Heavy Punch or Mega Punch
|}

Large damage needs correct form.

World Settings include Lightweight mode, Lightweight+ mode, Disable Custom FX, Hide watermark info, VRChat Settings Optimization, Rope Collision, and BGM (background music).

The world uses the [[Special:MyLanguage/Creator Economy|Creator Economy]]. The world store sells cosmetic gloves, Punch FX, and voice packs for [[Special:MyLanguage/Creator Economy#VRChat Credits|VRChat Credits]]. The official group store sells Silver, Gold, Platinum, and Diamond Supporter listings (1-month duration). Silver includes a Premium Glove. Gold includes the Premium Glove and VIP Room. Platinum and Diamond include those plus a Supporter List.

